diff --git a/docs/DECISIONS.md b/docs/DECISIONS.md
index 40d2f89..ee7c9e7 100644
--- a/docs/DECISIONS.md
+++ b/docs/DECISIONS.md
@@ -105,3 +105,4 @@ record for this repository; propose a change as a PR that adds a new entry
 | D-097 | 2026-10-25 | **Chart ranges, caption and headline belong to the product (`web/charts.py` `ChartSpec`).** A product's `ChartSpec` (default `DEFAULT_CHART`, overridden in `PRODUCT_CHARTS`) declares its range buttons, the default range, an optional caption and whether it is `daily`. `RANGE_CHOICES` gains `30d`, `90d`, `1y` and `all` ("todo", the whole store; always enabled, never chosen as the fallback default), offered only by products that declare them; `serie.json` accepts only the product's own ranges, anything else is its default. Buckets: 30 d 1 h, 90 d 3 h, 1 y and all 1 day, so a daily series is never averaged. `DAILY_CHART` (`noaa.goes.electron_fluence`): 30 días / 90 días / 1 año / todo, default 90 días (the coverage rule still applies: until 90 days are stored it opens on 30 días), caption "valores diarios (días UTC completos)" / "daily values (complete UTC days)" instead of "promedios de N min", and its latest datum reads "día 21/10" / "day 21 Oct", in the chart meta and under the headline (always, delayed or not), never a time. Any line with ≤ 60 values draws a marker on each one. | The fluence page offered 6 h–7 días (two points at its default, nothing at 6 h and 1 día), called its daily values 5-min averages and dated them 00:00 UT. | Victor / Claude |
 | D-098 | 2026-10-26 | **Flare collector reads flare-nrt 2.0 (`modules/flare/`).** When the producer's `/api/status` carries `observation_time`, it becomes the event's `valid_from` (the AIA slot the result is about); `issued` stays the producer's `timestamp`, so D-096's de-duplication is unchanged. `alert` and `event_id` are added to the payload, `model_version` and `data_latency_s` to `quality`, and `provenance` = `{"producer": "flare-nrt@<version>", "inputs": ["aia.synoptic <slot>"]}`. A 1.x payload parses exactly as before. The manifest is unchanged (`stale_after: 10m` = the producer's `STALE_AFTER_SEC` 600; it now updates every 2 min). The model card at `docs/products/usach.flare.nrt.md` is the producer's 2.0 card. | A result is made minutes after its observation (JSOC latency, now reported as `data_latency_s`); plotting it at processing time shifts every detection relative to the GOES curve it is read against. | Nicolás / Claude |
 | D-099 | 2026-10-26 | **The flare model is named Centella.** Its repository becomes `HelioUSACH/centella` (renamed from `flare-nrt`; GitHub redirects the old name), its units `centella-*.service`, and `provenance.producer` reads `centella@<version>`. The product id stays **`usach.flare.nrt`**: it names the product (flare detection, NRT), is already stored, exported and offered to the national platform, and a model can be replaced under it without breaking consumers. The manifest's `producer` field is updated accordingly; titles are unchanged. | Owner's decision. | Nicolás / Claude |
+| D-100 | 2026-10-27 | **The flare detector has its own page** (`web/flare_page.py`, `web/templates/web/product_detail_flare.html`), replacing the generic event page for `usach.flare.nrt`: current state (quiet / flare in progress / delayed / coming soon, from the latest event and the heartbeat), the 4 AIA channels as image or as the model's difference, the last 24 h of probability against GOES 0.1–0.8 nm flux, and the last 7 days of events with a GOES class taken from the stored X-ray peak in [start − 10 min, end + 10 min]. Everything is read from what the portal already stores, except the channel images: `productos/usach.flare.nrt/aia/<wave>.png` proxies Centella's `127.0.0.1` `/api/image/<wave>.png` (cached 60 s, 404 when the model is down; Centella stays unexposed, ARCHITECTURE §6). Charts are server-rendered SVG; the page reloads every 2 min with a meta refresh (no JS). | The mockup was approved; the generic page showed only the last event's issue time. | Nicolás / Claude |
